 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 520308,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure class=\"unnumbered\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/0ec25acad13ff175.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n<figcaption>(credit: modification of work by Tyler Warkentien and Rebecca Pavlicek/<i>Journal of Infectious Diseases and Epidemiology</i>, under CC BY 4.0 license)</figcaption>\n</figure>",
   "stem_html": "<p>Dengue fever is a viral disease carried between people by mosquitos. Dengue fever outbreaks were reported in 1635 and 1699. In World War II (1939-1945), Dengue fever, spread among the troops, was a major threat in the tropical Pacific. After 1945, the disease was largely contained. The graph shows the known cases of Dengue fever since 1955.</p>\n<p>What can be said about Dengue fever based on this data?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1016683,
     "content_html": "It is an emerging disease."
    },
    {
     "id": 1016684,
     "content_html": "It is a reemerging disease."
    },
    {
     "id": 1016685,
     "content_html": "It is a continuing pandemic for at least a century."
    },
    {
     "id": 1016686,
     "content_html": "It is completely eradicated in 1950s."
    }
   ],
